+*   **Memory Complexity:** Proportional to the number of model parameters and the batch size (storing gradients and optimizer states) [G].
 *   **Measured Performance:** Varies by implementation. For example, IBRNet baseline training takes 0.33 sec/iteration with 33.3 sec/frame rendering [S12, unofficial].
-*   **Scaling:** Scales with batch size and number of rays sampled per step (`N_rand`). Larger batches improve gradient stability but increase memory usage.
-*   **Strengths:** Flexible, supports various loss functions (L1, SSIM, Chamfer), and integrates with standard PyTorch/TensorFlow optimization utilities.
-*   **Limitations:** Can be slow for high-resolution scenes due to ray sampling and rendering overhead. Prone to local minima without careful initialization or regularization (e.g., importance sampling, adaptive loss weights).
